Run the dependent-parameter QR on the diagnosing thread, not a second one.

System::diagnose() starts identifyDependentParameters{Dense,Sparse}QR with
std::async's default policy, which libc++ runs on a new thread, and joins it
(fut.wait()) before reading its result. The result doesn't depend on
scheduling: the call works on copies of the Jacobian and its maps. Silico's
workers are single-threaded (ARCHITECTURE.md, Deterministic kernel, 5), so the
call is deferred: it runs on the calling thread at fut.wait(), with the same
arguments, giving the same result. FreeCAD's own comment above the sparse call
names std::launch::deferred as a supported policy.

Upstream: none yet (the maintainer files it). Drop when FreeCAD defers it, or
makes the policy configurable.

--- a/src/Mod/Sketcher/App/planegcs/GCS.cpp
+++ b/src/Mod/Sketcher/App/planegcs/GCS.cpp
@@ -4901,6 +4901,7 @@
         // identifyDependentParametersDenseQR(J, jacobianconstraintmap, pdiagnoselist, true)
         //
         auto fut = std::async(
+            std::launch::deferred,
             &System::identifyDependentParametersDenseQR,
             this,
             J,
@@ -4978,6 +4979,7 @@
         // std::async(std::launch::deferred,&System::identifyDependentParametersSparseQR, this,
         // J, jacobianconstraintmap, pdiagnoselist, false);
         auto fut = std::async(
+            std::launch::deferred,
             &System::identifyDependentParametersSparseQR,
             this,
             J,
